window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>CAN GUILT BE OVERCOME, OR WILL IT DESTROY EVERYTHING?</b></p> <p>In the eleventh volume of the Xane series, author Mark White delves into the complex and consuming emotion of guilt. Xane finds herself at the center of a storm when Ruby, a bandmate, reveals her deep-seated guilt over a logistical mistake that could jeopardize their upcoming tour performance. As Ruby struggles with the weight of her guilt, Xane must navigate the tension within the band and find a way to help her friend.</p> <p>Guided by the Analyst, Xane learns that <i>guilt can be both a motivator and a paralyzing force.</i> Through introspective conversations and challenging interactions with her bandmates, Xane discovers the importance of facing mistakes head-on, taking responsibility, and seeking solutions. As the band prepares for a high-stakes performance, they face technical difficulties and interpersonal conflicts that test their resilience and unity.</p> <p><i>Guilt </i>is a powerful exploration of emotional intelligence, highlighting the complexities of guilt and the importance of empathy, understanding, and forgiveness. Join Xane and her bandmates as they learn to navigate guilt, set emotional boundaries, and find strength in their journey. This volume is a must-listen for fans of the series and anyone interested in the intricate dance of emotions.</p>"; 
